{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107005","id":2557325027,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Yba7j","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107005","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107005.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107005.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107005","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107005/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107005/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107005/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/678fb63451f376a3140beba8246a026d9c0f1992","number":107005,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix ambiguous AnimationNode's parameter type in default value and make `validate_type_match()` static function","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105275\r\n- Supersedes/Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106440\r\n\r\nThe cause of this problem is the following implicit cast:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nVariant val = 0.0;\r\nWARN_PRINT(stringify_variant(val)); // 0.0\r\nval = 0;\r\nWARN_PRINT(stringify_variant(val)); // 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nConsidering the behavior of the Variant type, unless fundamental changes are made to the Variant type, it seems that the only solution is the approach suggested by @KoBeWi .\r\n\r\nThere are two places where problems occur:\r\n\r\n- `AnimationTree::_set()`\r\n- `AnimationNode::set_parameter()`\r\n\r\nHowever, even with these validations, the `property_map` may initially be set to the wrong type due to incorrect default parameter types.\r\n\r\nIn the former case `AnimationTree::_set()`, I assume that the type may have been saved incorrectly in past projects when the parameter was not changed after placing the AnimationNode. Below is an MRP that intentionally reproduces that situation.\r\n\r\n[replicate-tweening-blend-amount_issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20536567/replicate-tweening-blend-amount_issue.zip)\r\n\r\nIf you save that MRP after applying this PR, the stored type should be fixed in `cube.tscn`.\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes the type of the parameter's default value, adds validation, and makes the validation function static. Since the utilities related to Variant conversion are already collected in the Animation class, so I will integrate them there.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_